Cloud Run — What is it?

Cloud Run is a Google Cloud service that runs your application on the internet.

For example, you create a FastAPI application:

FastAPI Application
       ↓
Docker Container
       ↓
Cloud Run
       ↓
Live Website / API 🌐
Simple example

You have this project:

college-ai-assistant/
│
├── main.py
├── requirements.txt
└── Dockerfile

You deploy it to Cloud Run:

Your Code
   ↓
Cloud Build
   ↓
Docker Container
   ↓
Cloud Run
   ↓
https://your-app.run.app 🌐


========

What Cloud Run does

| Service               | Job                               |
| --------------------- | --------------------------------- |
| **Git**               | Tracks code changes               |
| **GitHub**            | Stores code online                |
| **Cloud Build**       | Builds your application/container |
| **Artifact Registry** | Stores Docker images              |
| **Cloud Run**         | Runs the application online       |


